      "Name": "body",
      "Html": "\u003Cstyle class=\u0022code-analysis-syntax\u0022\u003E\n.docs-content pre{overflow-x:auto;margin:1rem 0 1.75rem;padding:1.25rem 1.4rem;border:1px solid rgba(20,42,72,.16);border-left:4px solid #0e6fae;border-radius:4px;background:#f7fbfe;color:#10263a}\n.docs-content pre code{white-space:pre;color:inherit;background:transparent;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.65}\n.language-csharp .syntax-comment{color:#587287;font-style:italic}.language-csharp .syntax-string{color:#8a3d12}.language-csharp .syntax-keyword{color:#6542a6;font-weight:700}.language-csharp .syntax-number{color:#096b65}.language-csharp .syntax-type{color:#0a6680;font-weight:600}\n\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003EProperties may only be declared on models.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhat the Standard says\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026ldquo;Data Carrier Models\u0026rdquo; \u0026mdash; Data-carrier models exist to transport data points between parts of a system. Keeping behavior out of those models preserves that single purpose and leaves business operations in services. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://github.com/hassanhabib/The-Standard/blob/master/0.%20Introduction/0.1%20Purposing,%20Modeling%20\u0026%20Simulation.md#01200-data-carrier-models\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003Eread it here\u003C/a\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhy it matters\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EProperties represent carried state, which is the responsibility of models. Keeping them out of services and other functional elements preserves the Standard\u0027s distinction between data and behaviour and prevents service instances from acquiring hidden, long-lived state.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EBad code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Violates STX0002: Properties may only be declared on models.\u003C/span\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Einternal\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Einterface\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EIStudentService\u003C/span\u003E\n{\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E\u0026lt;\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ERetrieveStudent\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGuid\u003C/span\u003E studentId);\n}\n\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Einternal\u003C/span\u003E partial \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eclass\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudentService\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EIStudentBroker\u003C/span\u003E studentBroker) : \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EIStudentService\u003C/span\u003E\n{\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Epublic\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Estring\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStatus\u003C/span\u003E { get; set; }\n\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Epublic\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E\u0026lt;\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ERetrieveStudent\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGuid\u003C/span\u003E studentId) =\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ETryCatch\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Easync\u003C/span\u003E () =\u0026gt;\n    {\n        \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eawait\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValidate\u003C/span\u003E(studentId);\n\n        \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Ereturn\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eawait\u003C/span\u003E studentBroker.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ESelectStudentAsync\u003C/span\u003E(studentId);\n    });\n}\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EGood code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Follows STX0002\u003C/span\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Epublic\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eclass\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E\n{\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Epublic\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Estring\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStatus\u003C/span\u003E { get; set; }\n}\n\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Einternal\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Einterface\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EIStudentService\u003C/span\u003E\n{\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E\u0026lt;\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ERetrieveStudent\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGuid\u003C/span\u003E studentId);\n}\n\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Einternal\u003C/span\u003E partial \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eclass\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudentService\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EIStudentBroker\u003C/span\u003E studentBroker) : \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EIStudentService\u003C/span\u003E\n{\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Epublic\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E\u0026lt;\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ERetrieveStudent\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGuid\u003C/span\u003E studentId) =\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ETryCatch\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Easync\u003C/span\u003E () =\u0026gt;\n    {\n        \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eawait\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValidate\u003C/span\u003E(studentId);\n\n        \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Ereturn\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eawait\u003C/span\u003E studentBroker.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ESelectStudentAsync\u003C/span\u003E(studentId);\n    });\n}\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E"
    }
